// The pattern engine, written in Cufet.
//
// This file is bundled into the checker (see TypeChecker.WithPrelude): every program is checked and
// compiled as though it began with these statements.
//
// ★★ It declares NO module, and that is the point. A book on a LANGUAGE offers no members — you
// pull it to write patterns at all, not to call things on it — so the engine must not become
// `regex's match`. Everything here is a top-level helper, and BookLoading.MakePrivate renames each
// one after the book it belongs to: `match` becomes `match in regex`, a name with a space in it,
// which no identifier may contain. Unwritable, uncollidable, and reached only by the code the
// parser lowers a pattern into.
//
// ★★ Written in Cufet because the ORACLE requires it, not as a preference. Two engines — .NET's
// Regex interpreted and POSIX regcomp compiled — would disagree about greediness, character
// classes and empty matches, silently, on inputs nobody thought to test. The prelude is spliced in
// before either backend sees the program, so there is exactly one of this and nothing to diverge.
//
// ★ An AUTOMATON, never backtracking. A backtracking engine can hang forever on a pattern that
// looks fine; the usual defence is a timeout, and a timeout is nondeterministic where the oracle
// demands byte-for-byte agreement. It also matters more here than elsewhere: this engine is itself
// written in Cufet, so backtracking's worst case on a slow host is not "slow" but "never finishes".
//
// The compiled form is a series of records, built by RegexPattern.Compile:
//   kind 0 — match this character, then go to `step`
//   kind 1 — match any one character, then go to `step`
//   kind 2 — go to `step` or to `alt`, consuming nothing
//   kind 3 — accept
// `step` and `alt` are 1-based positions in the same series; 0 means nowhere. State 1 is the entry.
//
// ⚠ The four field names are a contract with RegexPattern.State, and nothing checks that the two
// agree. A change on either side is a change on both.

/// Marks `index` live, and follows every branch out of it that consumes nothing.
///
/// ⚠ The already-live check is what makes an epsilon CYCLE terminate — `(a*)*` reaches its own
/// branch again, and without this the walk would not stop.
Bind void to reach, given (
    the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) program,
    the number index,
    the series of fact active):
    If index is 0, return.
    If item index of active is true, return.
    The item index of active becomes true.
    Define node as item index of program.
    If the kind of node is 2:
        Cast reach on (program, the step of node, active).
        Cast reach on (program, the alt of node, active).
    Done.
Done.

/// Is any accepting state live?
Bind fact to accepting, given (
    the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) program,
    the series of fact active):
    Define index as 0.
    For each node in program, repeat:
        Increment index by 1.
        If item index of active is true:
            If the kind of node is 3, return true.
        Done.
    Done.
    Return false.
Done.

/// A fresh all-false liveness map, one entry per state.
Bind series of fact to blank, given (
    the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) program):
    Define flags as a series of fact.
    For each node in program, repeat:
        Insert false into flags.
    Done.
    Return flags.
Done.

/// Does `subject` hold a match for `program` anywhere in it?
///
/// ★ The set of live states is carried forward one character at a time, which is what makes the
/// cost linear in the subject however the pattern is shaped. `a*a*a*b` against a long run of a's
/// with no b — the input that makes a backtracking engine hang — is answered in one pass.
Bind fact to match, given (
    the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) program,
    the text subject):
    If the number of program is 0, return false.

    Define active as cast blank on (program).
    Cast reach on (program, 1, active).
    // Before consuming anything: a pattern that can match nothing at all matches here.
    If cast accepting on (program, active), return true.

    Define total as the length of subject.
    // ⚠ `range 1 to 0` COUNTS DOWN — it is `1, 0`, not empty — so without this an empty subject
    // would step to character position 0 and be refused. Documented behaviour, and a trap sitting
    // in the path of the most ordinary loop there is.
    If total is 0, return false.

    For each pos in range 1 to total, repeat:
        Define here as the characters from pos to pos of subject.
        Define onward as cast blank on (program).
        Define index as 0.
        For each node in program, repeat:
            Increment index by 1.
            If item index of active is true:
                If the kind of node is 0:
                    If the ch of node is here, cast reach on (program, the step of node, onward).
                Done.
                If the kind of node is 1:
                    Cast reach on (program, the step of node, onward).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        // Unanchored: a match may begin at any position, so the entry state is always live. This
        // is what makes the answer "does the subject HOLD a match", which is what slice 1's
        // `contains` lowering meant — the two must keep agreeing.
        Cast reach on (program, 1, onward).
        The active becomes onward.
        If cast accepting on (program, active), return true.
    Done.
    Return false.
Done.
